<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<BES xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="BES.xsd">
	<Analysis>
		<Title>YARA-X Scan Results - Universal</Title>
		<Description><![CDATA[<P>Reports the results of the &quot;Scan with YARA-X Signatures&quot; tasks (Windows, Linux, macOS), every hour, whatever signatures are deployed. Nothing here names a particular product: a signature is a rule file in the YARA engine signatures directory, and each one is loaded into its own namespace named after the file, so adding a signature adds to these results without any change to this analysis.</P><P>The scan tasks write two files into the YARA engine results directory, __BESData/__Global/__MitigationToolkit/yara/results:</P><P><CODE>yara_results_runtimes.text</CODE> - one TAB-separated line per match, &quot;signature&lt;TAB&gt;path&lt;TAB&gt;product&lt;TAB&gt;version&quot;. A file that matches more than one rule produces more than one line. Matches with no readable version are reported with version &quot;unknown&quot;.</P><P><CODE>yara_results_signatures.text</CODE> - one line per signature that was loaded for the scan, &quot;signature&lt;TAB&gt;count&quot;, including the signatures that matched nothing.</P><P>&quot;YARA Signature Results Count&quot; reports one result per signature, &quot;( signature, count )&quot;. &quot;YARA Result Details&quot; reports one result per match, &quot;( signature, path, product, version )&quot;. &quot;YARA per-signature Matches Found&quot; reports one result per matched signature. These are plural properties: each row is a separate result rather than one long string, so the console can filter and group on them.</P><P>Each result is built with the client's <CODE>tuple string</CODE> inspector, so values within a result are separated by &quot;, &quot; and the client escapes any comma or parenthesis inside a value &#8212; a path such as /opt/x, y comes back as &quot;( /opt/x, y )&quot;. Read them back with <CODE>tuple string items of</CODE> rather than splitting on commas by hand.</P><P>A computer is reported once a scan has written a results file. A computer that was scanned and matched nothing reports &quot;YARA Scan Matches Found&quot; as False.</P>]]></Description>
		<Relevance><![CDATA[exists files whose(name of it as lowercase starts with "yara_results_runtimes.text") of folders "results" of folders "yara" of folders "__MitigationToolkit" of folders "__Global" of data folders of client]]></Relevance>
		<Source>Internal</Source>
		<SourceID>jgstew</SourceID>
		<SourceReleaseDate>2026-11-17</SourceReleaseDate>
		<MIMEField>
			<Name>x-fixlet-modification-time</Name>
			<Value>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000</Value>
		</MIMEField>
		<Domain>BESC</Domain>
		<Property Name="YARA Scan Matches Found" ID="1" EvaluationPeriod="PT1H"><![CDATA[exists lines whose(it contains "%09") of files whose(name of it as lowercase starts with "yara_results_runtimes.text") of folders "results" of folders "yara" of folders "__MitigationToolkit" of folders "__Global" of data folders of client]]></Property>
		<Property Name="YARA per-signature Matches Found" ID="2" EvaluationPeriod="PT1H"><![CDATA[(tuple string of (it as string)) of (unique values of (preceding texts of firsts "%09" of lines of files whose(name of it as lowercase starts with "yara_results_runtimes.text") of folders "results" of folders "yara" of folders "__MitigationToolkit" of folders "__Global" of data folders of client))]]></Property>
		<Property Name="YARA Signature Results Count" ID="3" EvaluationPeriod="PT1H"><![CDATA[(tuple string of (it as string)) of ((tuple string of (it as string) of (substrings separated by "%09" of it)) of lines of files whose(name of it as lowercase starts with "yara_results_signatures.text") of folders "results" of folders "yara" of folders "__MitigationToolkit" of folders "__Global" of data folders of client)]]></Property>
		<Property Name="YARA Scan Time" ID="4" EvaluationPeriod="PT1H"><![CDATA[modification times of files whose(name of it as lowercase starts with "yara_results_runtimes.text") of folders "results" of folders "yara" of folders "__MitigationToolkit" of folders "__Global" of data folders of client]]></Property>
		<Property Name="YARA Result Details" ID="5" EvaluationPeriod="PT1H"><![CDATA[(tuple string of (it as string)) of ((tuple string of (it as string) of (substrings separated by "%09" of it)) of lines of files whose(name of it as lowercase starts with "yara_results_runtimes.text") of folders "results" of folders "yara" of folders "__MitigationToolkit" of folders "__Global" of data folders of client)]]></Property>
	</Analysis>
</BES>
